From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam <i@noc.cat>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 15:57:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 79/80] PCI: Avoid FLR and bus reset for the Toshiba TC956x Ethernet
 functions

The two Ethernet functions (1179:0220) of the Toshiba TC956x (Qualcomm
QPS615) PCIe switch advertise FLR, but after one the function never
becomes ready again. pci_dev_wait() gives up after 65 seconds, and on
the Radxa Dragon Q8B (SC8280XP) the config write pci_dev_restore() then
issues raises an asynchronous SError, which panics the machine.
vfio-pci resets a device this way when it is opened, so handing either
port to a guest took the host down.

Mark the functions NO_FLR_RESET. Mark them NO_BUS_RESET as well, so
that vfio-pci, finding no function reset, does not fall back to a
secondary bus reset of the downstream port they sit behind. Whether the
chip survives one has not been tested; a wrong guess costs the machine,
and the device driver puts the chip into a known state when it probes.

With no reset method left, both ports can be passed to a guest: the
guest's driver comes up with a 2.5 Gb/s link, and the VM can be started
and stopped repeatedly.
---
 drivers/pci/quirks.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/quirks.c b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
index 0500d5f..d183c46 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/quirks.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/quirks.c
@@ -3811,6 +3811,13 @@ DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_TI, 0xb005, quirk_no_bus_reset);
  */
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_ASMEDIA, 0x1164, quirk_no_bus_reset);
 
+/*
+ * The Ethernet functions of the Toshiba TC956x (QPS615) PCIe switch never
+ * become ready again after an FLR, and touching them afterwards takes the
+ * machine down. Keep vfio-pci from falling back to a bus reset as well.
+ */
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_HEADER(PCI_VENDOR_ID_TOSHIBA, 0x0220, quirk_no_bus_reset);
+
 static void quirk_no_pm_reset(struct pci_dev *dev)
 {
 	/*
@@ -5613,6 +5620,7 @@ DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_AMD, 0x17f0, quirk_no_flr);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x1502, quirk_no_flr);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_INTEL, 0x1503, quirk_no_flr);
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_MEDIATEK, 0x0616, quirk_no_flr);
+DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_TOSHIBA, 0x0220, quirk_no_flr); /* TC956x */
 DECLARE_PCI_FIXUP_EARLY(PCI_VENDOR_ID_MEDIATEK, 0x7925, quirk_no_flr);
 
 /* FLR may cause the SolidRun SNET DPU (rev 0x1) to hang */
